# Uldaros Theorix: "When Uldaros Theorix enters, if you cast him, exile up to one target nonland card of each card type from
# your graveyard. Copy those cards. You may cast any number of spells with total mana value 6 or less from among the copies
# without paying their mana costs." Bot1 fills its graveyard on turn 1 (Dark Ritual makes the mana for three Entombs, which
# take Ornithopter, Ponder and The Theorist, Jace Beleren; an Entomb shuffles, so what is left in the library is Swamps
# and the draws do not depend on the shuffle) and casts Uldaros on turn 5 with Black Lotus (blue), which is sacrificed for the
# mana and so is in the graveyard too. Its trigger takes an artifact (the Lotus), a creature (the Ornithopter), an
# instant (Dark Ritual), a planeswalker (Jace) and a sorcery (Ponder), all exiled. Bot1 then casts Jace (4), Ponder (1)
# and Dark Ritual (1): exactly 6, as many as are allowed - and the two cards of mana value 0, the Ornithopter and the Lotus,
# cost nothing more. A permanent spell cast this way becomes a token (CR 707.10f): the Jace, Ornithopter and Lotus
# on the battlefield are tokens, and the exiled cards they copy stay in exile. The Entombs are not chosen (one instant only
# is taken) and stay in the graveyard.

